      q: "A 6-year-old African American boy is brought to the physician because of easy fatigability. Physical examination reveals splenomegaly, and his complete blood count shows mild anemia. Hemoglobin electrophoresis is performed at alkaline pH on a cellulose acetate strip. Findings for the patient are shown below compared to individuals with normal hemoglobin and known sickle cell disease. Which of the following is the most likely cause of this patient’s condition?",
