      q: "An 8-month-old girl is brought to the office due to irritability and regression of motor skills. The patient’s birth was unremarkable and her development had appeared normal, but she can no longer sit or roll over. Her parents have also noticed that she startles easily at loud noises. Head circumference measurement is consistent with macrocephaly. Bilateral funduscopic evaluation shows a bright red fovea centralis that is surrounded by a contrasting white macula. Peripheral vision is decreased. Abdominal examination is normal. Accumulation of which of the following metabolites is most likely present in this patient’s tissues?",
